    title_en: "Japanese Cloud Provider IDCF Cloud Hit by Ransomware Attack, Multiple Client Service Areas Offline and Irrecoverable",
    summary_en: "IDCF Cloud, a service provided by IDC Frontier, was hit by a ransomware attack on October 7th in Japan time. The attack primarily affected four service areas in the East Japan Region—including tesla, henry, pascal, and joule—causing the virtual servers in that region to go offline and be unable to restart. Affected client data is difficult to retrieve or restore, and the provider advises clients to rely on self-saved backups for system reconstruction. Multiple clients were impacted, including Six Apart, the developer of the website content management system Movable Type, whose 31 servers were forced to be migrated to Sakura Cloud for reconstruction. Additionally, other affected entities include Nissui's subsidiary, Nisui Logistics, the wholesale trading platform NETSEA, and the official website of Ibaraki Prefecture government. IDC Frontier has disconnected the affected region's network connection and has reported the incident to regulatory authorities and the Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department. Investigations are ongoing regarding the intrusion methods and data leakage status.",
    tags_en: ["IDC Frontier", "IDCF Cloud", "Ransomware", "Japanese Cloud", "Data Leakage", "Virtual Server"],
