    category: "Linux",
    title: "NVIDIA 提出 Linux 核心 AI Agent 資源提案，旨在提升補丁自動化標記與開發效率",
    summary: "NVIDIA 的 Sasha Levin 提交了一項關於 Linux 核心的重大提案，旨在引入 AI Agent 資源基礎設施。此提案的核心目的是建立一個專門的目錄（如 `agents/`），用來集中收集未來用於程式輔助工具（coding assistants）的技能、提示（prompts）和其他資源。初期規劃的技能是利用大型語言模型（LLMs）來自動判斷和添加「Fixes: 」標籤，以便精確記錄一個新的補丁修復了 Linux 核心的哪個特定 Commit。這項提案顯示了 AI 技術正深度整合到 Linux 核心的開發流程中，涵蓋了自動化標記、AI 驅動的合併衝突解決，以及利用 AI 輔助將補丁回溯到舊版核心。這將極大地提升核心維護和開發的效率，但其最終的實施與採用程度仍有待觀察。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "AI Agent", "NVIDIA", "LLMs", "補丁管理", "開發工具鏈"],
    title_en: "NVIDIA Proposes Linux Kernel AI Agent Resources to Enhance Patch Automation and Development Efficiency",
    summary_en: "NVIDIA's Sasha Levin submitted a significant proposal for the Linux kernel, aiming to introduce an AI Agent resource infrastructure. The core purpose of this proposal is to establish a dedicated directory (such as `agents/`) to centralize skills, prompts, and other resources intended for future coding assistants. The initial planned capability is to utilize Large Language Models (LLMs) to automatically detect and add \"Fixes: \" tags, thereby precisely documenting which specific Commit a new patch remedies in the Linux kernel. This proposal demonstrates the deep integration of AI technology into the Linux kernel development workflow, encompassing automated tagging, AI-driven merge conflict resolution, and using AI assistance to backport patches to older kernel versions. While this promises to greatly enhance core maintenance and development efficiency, its ultimate implementation and adoption remain to be seen.",
