    summary_en: "Google has released Android 17 QPR2 Beta 7, available for testing on Pixel devices. The devices covered by this version include Pixel 6a, Pixel 7, Pixel 7 Pro, Pixel 7a, Pixel Tablet, Pixel Fold, Pixel 8, Pixel 8 Pro, Pixel 8a, Pixel 9, Pixel 9 Pro, Pixel 9 Pro XL, Pixel 9 Pro Fold, Pixel 9a, Pixel 10, Pixel 10 Pro, Pixel 10 Pro XL, Pixel 10 Pro Fold, Pixel 10a, Pixel 11, Pixel 11 Pro, Pixel 11 Pro XL, and Pixel 11 Pro Fold, as well as the Android Emulator. This Beta 7 version primarily fixes two issues: first, the device failing to enter deep sleep when using the \"Flip to Shh\" function, which caused excessive battery drain; and second, HTTPS downloads initiated via the system DownloadManager immediately failing. Users can report issues through the Android Beta Feedback app or the Reddit community. Users are advised to quickly install Beta 7 onto devices currently running Beta 6.1 via Sideloading.",
