    title_en: "Apple Acquires AI Project Huxe and Team via 'Acqui-hire' Model from Former Google NotebookLM Developers",
    summary_en: "According to public data from the EU's Digital Markets Act, Apple has reached a cooperation agreement with the AI application Huxe. The Huxe team consists of former Google NotebookLM developers. The application was initially designed to generate personalized audio briefings and provide podcast-style content using users' emails and calendars. While this is not a direct corporate acquisition, it is a typical 'Acqui-hire' model, through which Apple secured the employment of Huxe's key personnel and obtained a non-exclusive license to its intellectual property. This aligns with Apple's recent strategy of acquiring AI-related companies to expand its capabilities in voice and visual interface interaction technologies. Notably, this type of talent acquisition model has drawn regulatory attention, with the US FTC and Department of Justice beginning to consider modifying relevant merger reporting rules to address such transactions.",
