    title_en: "Volkswagen Announces ID. Tiguan as Successor to ID.4, Utilizing MEB+ Platform and Enhanced Performance",
    summary_en: "Volkswagen has announced the discontinuation of the ID.4 mid-sized crossover and introduced the ID. Tiguan as its successor. The ID. Tiguan combines successful elements of both the ID.4 and ID.5, built upon the updated MEB+ electric vehicle platform. The model offers two battery options: 58 kWh or 77 kWh. With the 58 kWh battery, it features a rear electric motor producing 187 hp (140 kW); while the 77 kWh battery allows for a rear-wheel-drive version with 281 hp (210 kW) or an all-wheel-drive version with 295 hp (220 kW). According to European WLTP testing, the maximum range can reach 373 miles (600 km). Through the ID. Tiguan, VW aims to enhance the vehicle's exterior and interior quality, positioning it closer to the luxury market segment.",
