    title: "美國海軍投資 X-BAT 無跑道戰鬥無人機：實現跨平台、垂直起降的戰力提升",
    summary: "美國國防公司 Shield AI 宣布，美國海軍將額外投入 1.5 億美元，用於推進其自主垂直起降（VTOL）戰鬥無人機 X-BAT 的飛行測試。X-BAT 旨在為海軍指揮官提供長程打擊資產，使其能夠從幾乎任何地方垂直起飛和著陸，從根本上擺脫對傳統跑道的依賴。該無人機預計具備超音速飛行能力，航程超過 2,000 海里，長度為 26 呎，翼展為 39 呎。如果投入使用，X-BAT 將使美國海軍能夠從大型航空母艦（如 USS Gerald R. Ford）以外的船隻，如遠征海基（ESB），操作戰鬥機。X-BAT 採用尾部固定式（tail-sitter）設計，並將由 Shield AI 的 Hivemind 自主軟體控制。此外，英國皇家海軍也在進行類似的戰鬥無人機採購計畫（Project VANQUISH），這使得 X-BAT 有潛力成為該計畫的候選機型。",
    tags: ["Shield AI", "X-BAT", "美國海軍", "VTOL", "無人機", "國防科技"],
    title_en: "US Navy Invests in X-BAT Unmanned Combat Aircraft: Enhancing Combat Capability with Cross-Platform, Vertical Takeoff and Landing",
    summary_en: "Defense contractor Shield AI announced that the US Navy will invest an additional $150 million to advance flight testing of the X-BAT, its autonomous Vertical Takeoff and Landing (VTOL) combat drone. X-BAT is designed to provide naval commanders with long-range strike assets, enabling it to take off and land vertically from virtually any location, fundamentally eliminating reliance on traditional runways. The drone is expected to feature supersonic flight capabilities, a range exceeding 2,000 nautical miles, a length of 26 feet, and a wingspan of 39 feet. If deployed, X-BAT would allow the US Navy to operate fighter aircraft from vessels other than large aircraft carriers (such as the USS Gerald R. Ford), including Expeditionary Sea Bases (ESB). X-BAT utilizes a tail-sitter design and will be controlled by Shield AI's Hivemind autonomous software. Furthermore, the British Royal Navy is undertaking a similar combat drone procurement program (Project VANQUISH), giving X-BAT the potential to become a candidate for that program.",
