    summary_en: "Through a Surface Store trade-in program, Microsoft has launched the Surface Laptop Ultra, positioning it as a competitor to the MacBook Pro and offering high trade-in credits to attract Apple users. The promotion runs from October 7 to November 23, 2026, allowing users to trade in their MacBook Pro and receive up to $1,000 in cash back. The Surface Laptop Ultra is equipped with the RTX Spark chip, combining a 20-core Grace CPU with up to a 6,144-core Blackwell GPU, and supports CUDA cores. This presents a difference in software ecosystem compared to Apple's Metal/MLX. Furthermore, Microsoft has introduced Microsoft Execution Containers (MXC) in Windows 11, used to define the access permissions for AI agents at the operating system level, strengthening Windows 11's position as an AI application platform. Although the Surface Laptop Ultra offers diverse interfaces (such as USB-A ports and replaceable SSDs), a price comparison with the MacBook Pro shows that the price difference is minimal for similar memory and storage capacities. The final decision point thus rests on the trade-in value and the choice of software ecosystem.",
