    title_en: "EU Scientific Panel Holds Special Meeting to Assess Frontier AI Systemic Risks and Loss-of-Control Incidents",
    summary_en: "The European Commission convened a special meeting of its Scientific Panel on Artificial Intelligence (AI), focusing on assessing the safety and risks associated with frontier AI. The panel, composed of 60 world-class independent experts, provides professional advice to the EU AI Office and national authorities regarding systemic risks, model classification, evaluation methodologies, and cross-border market regulation. The meeting specifically addressed recent 'loss-of-control incidents' and prepared a series of questions for companies developing related models. European Executive Vice-President Henna Virkkunen emphasized that while AI capabilities are advancing rapidly, the EU possesses the world's first legal framework for managing AI systemic risks. By combining advanced scientific input with strict enforcement, the EU aims to maintain a leading position in safe and reliable AI development. The panel will submit concrete recommendations to the Commission concerning the safety and systemic risks of frontier AI, thereby strengthening the implementation of the AI Act.",
